{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task SE-PE-01 is about grammar-guided node reduction on a parse tree. Let me understand the requirements:\n\n1. We have a tree of nodes, each with: id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility\n2. We have required_symbols that must always be present in the retained nodes\n3. We need to reduce the tree by removing nodes while:\n   - Never removing the root\n   - Never removing a node with a required symbol\n   - Never removing a node with retained children\n   - Only removing a node if all required symbols remain represented after removal\n   - Considering deeper nodes before shallower nodes\n   - Using node ID as stable tiebreak at equal depth\n\nLet me trace through the first fixture to understand the logic:\n\nCase 000:\n- Nodes: root(depth=0), n1(depth=1,s1,not removable), n2(depth=1,s2,removable), n3(depth=1,s0,not removable), n4(depth=2,s1,removable,parent=n2), n5(depth=2,s2,not removable,parent=n3), n6(depth=2,s0,removable,parent=n1)\n- Required symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nThe algorithm should:\n1. Sort nodes by depth (deepest first), then by node ID as tiebreak\n2. For each node in this order, tentatively try to remove it\n3. A node can be removed if:\n   - It's removable\n   - It has no retained children\n   - All required symbols remain represented after removal\n\nLet me think about the \"registered_candidate_order\" - it says to consider deeper nodes first, with node ID as tiebreak.\n\nAt depth 2: n4(s1,removable), n5(s2,not removable), n6(s0,removable)\nAt depth 1: n1(s1,not removable), n2(s2,removable), n3(s0,not removable)\nAt depth 0: root(not removable)\n\nSo the order of consideration (depth desc, then id asc):\n- n4 (depth 2), n5 (depth 2), n6 (depth 2), then n1 (depth 1), n2 (depth 1), n3 (depth 1), root (depth 0)\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" And \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\"\n\nSo order: sort by depth descending, then by node ID ascending (lexicographic).\n\nDepth 2 nodes: n4, n5, n6 (by ID: n4, n5, n6)\nDepth 1 nodes: n1, n2, n3\nDepth 0 nodes: root\n\nNow let's process:\n\nStart: all nodes retained. \nRequired symbols: {root, s1}\nCurrent symbols represented: root(root), s1(n1,n4), s2(n2,n5), s0(n3,n6)\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, symbol=s1, removable=True, parent=n2):\n- Check: removable? Yes\n- Check: no retained children? n4 has no children, so yes\n- Check: if we remove n4, do all required symbols remain? \n  - root: still present (root node)\n  - s1: n1 still has s1, so yes\n- So we CAN remove n4. Remove it.\n- removal_order: [n4]\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, symbol=s2, removable=False):\n- Not removable. Skip.\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, symbol=s0, removable=True, parent=n1):\n- Check: removable? Yes\n- Check: no retained children? n6 has no children, yes\n- Check: if we remove n6, do all required symbols remain?\n  - root: yes\n  - s1: n1 still has s1\n- So we CAN remove n6. Remove it.\n- removal_order: [n4, n6]\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, symbol=s1, removable=False):\n- Not removable. Skip.\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, symbol=s2, removable=True, parent=root):\n- Check: removable? Yes\n- Check: no retained children? n4 was removed, so n2 has no retained children. Yes.\n- Check: if we remove n2, do all required symbols remain?\n  - root: yes\n  - s1: n1 has s1, yes\n- So we CAN remove n2. Remove it.\n- removal_order: [n4, n6, n2]\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, symbol=s0, removable=False):\n- Not removable. Skip.\n\nProcess root (depth=0, removable=False):\n- Not removable. Skip.\n\nFinal:\n- removed: [n4, n6, n2]\n- retained: [root, n1, n3, n5]\n\nWait, but the output says \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" So retained_node_ids should be sorted (lexicographically? by what?). Let me re-read.\n\n\"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\"\n\nSo retained_node_ids is sorted (probably alphabetically or by some order), and removed_node_ids is in the actual order of removal.\n\nFor the retained: {root, n1, n3, n5} - sorted: n1, n3, n5, root (if alphabetical)... or maybe numerically? Let me think about what \"sorted\" means here. Probably lexicographic string sort.\n\nLexicographic: \"n1\" \u003c \"n3\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"root\"\n\nSo retained_node_ids = [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\nremoved_node_ids = [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"] (in removal order)\n\nLet me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate\n    if not nodes:\n        raise ValueError(\"No nodes in case\")\n    \n    # Build lookup structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            if n[\"parent\"] not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {n['parent']} not found\")\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Check required symbols exist in nodes\n    existing_symbols = {n[\"symbol\"] for n in nodes}\n    for sym in required_symbols:\n        if sym not in existing_symbols:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Required symbol {sym} not found in any node\")\n    \n    # Sort candidates: deepest first, then by node ID (lexicographic)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    # Track retained set\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removal_order = []\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if has retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c in retained for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Try removing: check if all required symbols remain\n        # Symbols represented after removal = symbols of retained nodes except this one\n        # We need to check if required symbols are covered\n        \n        # Count symbol coverage\n        # After removing nid, symbols covered = {node_map[r][\"symbol\"] for r in retained if r != nid}\n        retained_after = retained - {nid}\n        symbols_after = {node_map[r][\"symbol\"] for r in retained_after}\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(symbols_after):\n            # Remove this node\n            retained.remove(nid)\n            removal_order.append(nid)\n    \n    # Sort retained IDs\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nWait, computing symbols_after for each candidate by iterating all retained nodes is O(n^2). For small cases this is fine. But we could optimize with a symbol counter. Let me use a counter approach for cleanliness:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    \n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    if not nodes:\n        raise ValueError(\"No nodes in case\")\n    \n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = defaultdict(list)\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            if n[\"parent\"] not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {n['parent']} not found\")\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Check required symbols exist\n    existing_symbols = {n[\"symbol\"] for n in nodes}\n    for sym in required_symbols:\n        if sym not in existing_symbols:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Required symbol {sym} not found\")\n    \n    # Symbol count among retained nodes\n    symbol_count = defaultdict(int)\n    retained = set()\n    for n in nodes:\n        retained.add(n[\"id\"])\n        symbol_count[n[\"symbol\"]] += 1\n    \n    # Sort: deepest first, then by node ID lexicographic\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removal_order = []\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check no retained children\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Check if required symbols remain after removal\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_count[sym] \u003c= 1:\n            # Removing this would drop a required symbol\n            continue\n        \n        # Remove this node\n        retained.discard(nid)\n        symbol_count[sym] -= 1\n        removal_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nThis is cleaner and more efficient.\n\nLet me trace through case 000 again with this:\n\nInitial symbol_count: root:1, s1:2(n1,n4), s2:2(n2,n5), s0:2(n3,n6)\nRequired: {root, s1}\n\nsorted_nodes by (-depth, id): n4, n5, n6, n1, n2, n3, root\n\nn4: removable=True, children of n4=[], sym=s1, symbol_count[s1]=2 \u003e 1 → remove n4\n  retained: {root,n1,n2,n3,n5,n6}, symbol_count[s1]=1, removal=[n4]\n\nn5: removable=False → skip\n\nn6: removable=True, children of n6=[], sym=s0, s0 not in required_symbols → remove n6\n  retained: {root,n1,n2,n3,n5}, symbol_count[s0]=1, removal=[n4,n6]\n\nn1: removable=False → skip\n\nn2: removable=True, children of n2=[n4], n4 not in retained → no retained children. sym=s2, not required → remove n2\n  retained: {root,n1,n3,n5}, symbol_count[s2]=1, removal=[n4,n6,n2]\n\nn3: removable=False → skip\n\nroot: removable=False → skip\n\nFinal:\nretained_sorted = sorted({root,n1,n3,n5}) = [\"n1\",\"n3\",\"n5\",\"root\"]\nremoved = [\"n4\",\"n6\",\"n2\"]\n\nThis looks right!\n\nLet me also trace case 001:\nNodes: same structure as 000, different utilities.\nRequired: {root, s1}\n\nn4(depth=2,s1,removable), n5(depth=2,s2,not removable), n6(depth=2,s0,removable), n1(depth=1,s1,not removable), n2(depth=1,s2,removable), n3(depth=1,s0,not removable), root(depth=0,not removable)\n\nInitial symbol_count: root:1, s1:2, s2:2, s0:2\n\nn4: removable, no children, s1 count=2\u003e1 → remove. symbol_count[s1]=1, removal=[n4]\nn5: not removable → skip\nn6: removable, no children, s0 not required → remove. removal=[n4,n6]\nn1: not removable → skip\nn2: removable, children=[n4] not in retained → remove s2 not required → remove. removal=[n4,n6,n2]\nn3: not removable → skip\nroot: not removable → skip\n\nSame result as case 000: retained=[n1,n3,n5,root], removed=[n4,n6,n2]\n\nCase 002:\nSame structure. Same result expected.\n\nNow let me format as the required JSON output with the implementation as a string:\n\nThe implementation string needs proper JSON escaping.\n\nLet me write the final implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    \n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    if not nodes:\n        raise ValueError(\"No nodes in case\")\n    \n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = defaultdict(list)\n    for n in nodes:\n        p = n[\"parent\"]\n        if p is not None:\n            if p not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {p} not found in node map\")\n            children[p].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    existing_symbols = {n[\"symbol\"] for n in nodes}\n    for sym in required_symbols:\n        if sym not in existing_symbols:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Required symbol '{sym}' not represented in any node\")\n    \n    symbol_count = defaultdict(int)\n    retained = set()\n    for n in nodes:\n        retained.add(n[\"id\"])\n        symbol_count[n[\"symbol\"]] += 1\n    \n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removal_order = []\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_count[sym] \u003c= 1:\n            continue\n        \n        retained.discard(nid)\n        symbol_count[sym] -= 1\n        removal_order.append(nid)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nNow I need to produce the exact output format: a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" whose value is this Python source as a JSON string.\n\nLet me write the JSON-encoded version carefully.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    from collections import defaultdict\\n\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    if not nodes:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"No nodes in case\\\")\\n\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = defaultdict(list)\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n[\\\"parent\\\"]\\n        if p is not None:\\n            if p not in node_map:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Parent '{p}' not found in node map\\\")\\n            children[p].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    existing_symbols = {n[\\\"symbol\\\"] for n in nodes}\\n    for sym in required_symbols:\\n        if sym not in existing_symbols:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Required symbol '{sym}' not represented in any node\\\")\\n\\n    symbol_count = defaultdict(int)\\n    retained = set()\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        retained.add(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n        symbol_count[n[\\\"symbol\\\"]] += 1\\n\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    removal_order = []\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        sym = node[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_count[sym] \u003c= 1:\\n            continue\\n\\n        retained.discard(nid)\\n        symbol_count[sym] -= 1\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removal_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01DQqZB46eVS80SVeyd54UUA","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2536,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":54,"output_tokens":4091,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3621},"service_tier":"standard"}}